{
  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n1. Pod logs of `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` report repeated `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire ...s)`.\n2. Deployment `billing-api` configures `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900` in `spec.template.spec.containers[0].env`.\n3. Resource `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` in namespace `ack-system` defines `spec.idleClientTimeout: 600` following deployment `CI-2452`.\n\n### Leads Ruled Out\n1. Application memory leak (INC-2025-0918) was ruled out because memory is capped below limits and pod restarts/OOMKills are zero.\n2. Load balancer idle timeout issue (INC-2025-0611) was ruled out because deployment CI-2455 previously raised ALB timeout to 120s.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe DBProxy idle connection timeout (600s) is shorter than billing-api's pool idle timeout (900s), causing proxy drops (per RB-014).\n\n### Recommended Action\nThe infrastructure team should raise `spec.idleClientTimeout` on `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` above 900s, or the billing team lower `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`.",
